uartered in Chicago. Equity LifeStyle Properties, Inc. was incorporated in 1992 in Maryland and based in Chicago, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Marguerite M. Nader | CEO & Non-Independent Vice Chairman | Age 56 | Compensation: $2.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $414K ranks in the bottom quartile among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $90K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Equity Lifestyle Properties, In is a large-cap real estate business with a $12.5B market cap on $1.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $334M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 22 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.42\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 3.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 76% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7639639469641339},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.4% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["33 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Elsight (ASX:ELS) Shares in Focus: Why Is the ASX 200 Stock on the Radar?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/artificial-intelligence/elsight-asxels-shares-in-focus-why-is-the-asx-200-stock-on-the-radar","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794552000.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.077,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Elsight (ASX:ELS) Shares in Focus: Why Is the ASX 20